    <div class="flow">
      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">How to set up your paper</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Draw the stack as a column. Write new vertices on top; cross out the top when you pop.</li>
          <li>Write the DFS order as you <b>push</b> each vertex.</li>
          <li>On the drawing, trace each step with a pencil so you can see the dead ends.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="paper flow">
        <p class="note-label">Problem 1</p>
        <p>This is the same graph as Problem 1 in the BFS lesson.</p>
        <GraphFig g={p1} label="Practice graph 1, undirected, vertices A to G" />
        <ol>
          <li>Do a DFS starting at <b>D</b> (neighbors in alphabetical order). Write the DFS order.</li>
          <li>Compare it with your BFS order from D.</li>
        </ol>
        <details class="reveal">
          <summary>Show the answer</summary>
          <div class="flow">
            <p><b>DFS order:</b> <span class="mono">{r1.order.join(', ')}</span></p>
            <p><b>BFS order</b> (from the BFS lesson): <span class="mono">{r1b.order.join(', ')}</span></p>
            <p>The trace, one row per push or pop. Each row shows the same stack, one step later (bottom → top, left to right):</p>
            <div class="tbl-wrap">
              <table class="tbl small">
                <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Stack (bottom → top)</th><th>DFS order so far</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>{r1Rows.map((r, i) => <tr><td>{i + 1}</td><td class="nowrap">{r.act}</td><td class="mono nowrap">{r.stack}</td><td class="mono nowrap">{r.order}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <p>DFS went D → B → A → C → E → F before backing up. F was a dead end (D and E visited), so it popped back through E, C, A, and B to D, which still had G unvisited.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="paper flow">
        <p class="note-label">Problem 2 (directed)</p>
        <GraphFig g={p2} label="Practice graph 2, directed, vertices A to F" />
        <ol>
          <li>Do a DFS starting at <b>C</b>, following the arrows. Write the DFS order.</li>
