      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>DFS goes as deep as possible, then backtracks at dead ends.</li>
          <li>It uses a <b>stack</b> (or recursion). Push = go deeper; pop = go back.</li>
          <li>Write a vertex in the order when you first visit it.</li>
          <li>DFS finds everything reachable and can find <i>a</i> path, but not always the shortest.</li>
          <li>BFS = broad, queue, shortest path. DFS = deep, stack, follows one path to its end before trying another.</li>
        </ol>
